MGn) is coupled to a memory controller 10 and in which, in an embodiment shown by LeeSVG14940084.04-18-2017.J1NWFDVTRXEAPX2.REM.1.19.305.1849.360.1861.svg0.040.183ChemistryBlack and whiteFigure 11, two memories within a given memory group may concurrently output read data onto respective sets of data lines (rdl, rd2) within that memory group (Lee, paragraphs 0083-0087, referring to Figure 11). Even assuming arguendo that Lee's memory groups MG1 and MG2 correspond respectively to the first plurality of the memory components and the second plurality of the memory components recited in applicant's independent claims (i.e., as posited in Office Action Section 5), Lee's first memory group (MG1) clearly does not include any memory component that is also included in the second memory group (MG2). Nor would it be obvious to modify Lee to achieve such an arrangement as Lee's first and second memory groups are presented and describedas entirely distinct entities in all disclosed SVG14940084.04-18-2017.J1NWFDVTRXEAPX2.REM.1.28.1149.2584.1431.2631.svg0.1570.94ChemistryBlack and white .
