Claim Rejections - 35 USC § 103
Claims 3, 5, 10, 13 and 15 have been rejected under pre-AIA 35 U.S.C. § 103(a) as being unpatentable over Lee in view of U.S. Pre-Grant Publication No. 2007/0088995 ("Tsern").
Tsern is directed to a buffered memory module in which individual groups of memory devices are accessed through respective buffering devices (see embodiments shown in Tsern Figures 1-8 and accompanying description). However, like Lee, Tsern does not disclose the above- recited feature of amended claims 1, 11 and 20 so that, even if Lee and Tsern could be combined as proposed in the Office Action, the combination would still lack one or more features incorporated by dependency into claims 3, 5 10, 13 and 15 and therefore fail to establish a prima facie case of obviousness with respect to those claims. Accordingly, Applicant respectfully requests that the section 103 rejections be withdrawn.
Reasons Not Exhaustive
